Scope note: the MIT grant above covers the material authored in this
repository -- the harness under `trackii/`, the tests, the research and audit
scripts under `research/`, the case files under `cases/`, the generated site,
and the documentation.

It does not and cannot extend to the third-party documents reproduced under
`corpus/`. Those are source texts, committed so that quotations in the
methodology can be checked against them. They are US Government works in the
public domain (Congressional Research Service, USTR, USCC, the National
Security Strategy) and official texts of the People's Republic of China
(Ministry of Commerce and Ministry of Foreign Affairs statements, the
Anti-Secession Law, the Export Control Law, the Anti-Foreign Sanctions Law,
white papers). Each carries whatever status its own origin gives it. Copyrighted
third-party analysis is deliberately not redistributed here; `research/MANIFEST.md`
and `research/CORPUS.sha256` let you fetch and verify those yourself.
